from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,re,difflib,shutil
r=Path(r'C:/Users/OPERATOR/AppData/Local/Temp/nbsr-kar-positive-20261012');e=Path(r'C:/Users/OPERATOR/AppData/Local/Temp/nbsr-kar-positive-evidence-20261012');b=Path(r'C:/Users/OPERATOR/AppData/Local/Temp/nbsr-publication-validation-20261011');o=Path(r'C:/Users/OPERATOR/OneDrive/Documents/NBSR/evidence/local-handoff/2026-10-12');sha=lambda x:hashlib.sha256(x).hexdigest();base=json.loads((e/'source-manifest.json').read_text());pins={x['path']:x for x in base['files']};names=set();groups=[]
for patch in ['kar-positive.patch','sphere-offline.patch','sphere-cleanup.patch']:
 lines=(e/patch).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True);i=0;g=[]
 while i<len(lines):
  if not lines[i].startswith('--- '):i+=1;continue
  n=lines[i+1][6:].strip().replace('\\','/');names.add(n);i+=2;h=[]
  while i<len(lines) and not lines[i].startswith('--- '):
   if not lines[i].startswith('@@'):i+=1;continue
   m=re.match(r'@@ -(\d+)(?:,(\d+))? \+(\d+)(?:,(\d+))?',lines[i]);i+=1;t=[]
   while i<len(lines) and not lines[i].startswith(('@@','--- ')):t.append(lines[i]);i+=1
   h.append((m,t))
  g.append((n,h))
 groups.append(g)
old={n:(r/n).read_text(encoding='utf-8').splitlines(True) for n in names}
for g in reversed(groups):
 for n,h in g:
  for m,t in reversed(h):
   pos=int(m[3])-1 if int(m[4] or 1) else int(m[3]);new=[x[1:] for x in t if x[0] in ' +'];prev=[x[1:] for x in t if x[0] in ' -'];assert old[n][pos:pos+len(new)]==new,(n,pos);old[n][pos:pos+len(new)]=prev
corrections=[];patch='';bad=[]
for n in sorted(names):
 before=''.join(old[n]).encode()
 if n in pins:
  candidates=[before,before.replace(b'\n',b'\r\n')]
  if (b/n).exists():candidates += [(b/n).read_bytes()]
  exact=next((v for v in candidates if sha(v)==pins[n]['sha256']),None)
  if exact is None:bad.append(n);continue
  if exact!=before:corrections.append(n)
  before=exact
 else:assert not before,n
 patch+=''.join(difflib.unified_diff(before.decode().splitlines(True),(r/n).read_bytes().decode().splitlines(True),fromfile='a/'+n,tofile='b/'+n))
 dest=o/'files'/n;dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copyfile(r/n,dest)
assert not bad,bad
(o/'combined-ad77.patch').write_text(patch,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
print('verified',len(names),'corrections',corrections)
for p in e.rglob('*'):
 if p.is_file():
  dest=o/'evidence'/p.relative_to(e);dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True);shutil.copyfile(p,dest)
for n in ['nbsr-kar-positive-check.py','nbsr-ci-clean-check.py','nbsr-build-handoff.py']:shutil.copyfile(e.parent/n,o/'evidence'/n)
(o/'README.md').write_text('''# Local handoff — 2026-10-12

Base ad77d59754651fee449bb1d9c14a946f9f3b2d15; tree 106fb549a4088681b318cc57c3ed00754e4c925e.
Uncommitted, unpublished. Original checkout files preserved; bundle is additive.

Use combined-ad77.patch against the exact base, or inspect final files/ snapshots.
All 24 changed/new paths were verified: old-side bytes match the baseline SHA-256
inventory (including original line endings), and new paths reverse to empty.
Historical individual patches remain unchanged in evidence/, not recommended for
replay: sphere-offline.patch has Windows headers and treats the existing SPHERE
runbook as new. Combined patch corrects this using exact hash-verified baseline.
Do not apply both combined and historical patches. No build caches, binaries,
partial packs or private keys were copied. Test material is public deterministic
fixture material. Local retention does not authorize publication.

Offline SPHERE README/result source-match claims describe their earlier snapshot;
cleanup subsequently changed coordinator sources. Historical hashes/results are
preserved. Current identity is base plus combined patch and inventory.json.
CONFIG_VALID_OFFLINE does not mean READY or runtime authority.

Counts are non-additive: KAR retained 89 unique Python neighbors, 19 native tests
(12 KAR, 6 signature, 1 control), checker 4 positive/18 negative cases. SPHERE
retained 16 selected tests and 5 config rejection cases. Cleanup retained 56+10=66
unique tests. Consolidation reran the SAME 66 together, checker and preflight:
all passed. Do not sum overlapping suites or retries. Earlier failures, warnings,
resource aborts and retries remain retained. No native rebuild during handoff.
Independent combined review found no code interaction defect; portability and
historical-source wording issues are addressed here. Copy integrity is verified
by inventory.json, not by the independent reviewer.

Original cumulative disk baseline remains 14,247,788,544 bytes, 2 GiB growth cap;
no budget reset. All consolidation workers reaped without abort. Exact commands,
resource readings and elapsed times are retained in handoff-* logs.

Next three gates:
1. Review combined local changes; decide whether to authorize the narrow watchdog
   implementation described in WATCHDOG-DESIGN.md.
2. Implement/review deterministic watchdog and remote-proof failure handling;
   separately authorize any exact live test resources and SSH/socket use.
3. Approve allocation, SSH trust, Linux build/TLS provenance and resource limits
   before bounded live validation. Registration governance/runtime authority is
   a separate unmet requirement. No live readiness or publication is claimed.
''',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
(o/'WATCHDOG-DESIGN.md').write_text('''# Whole-trial watchdog acceptance — design only

One owner, one immutable monotonic deadline covering startup, management, collection
and cleanup. Under an authorized 120-second cap, begin cleanup by 95–105 seconds;
every subordinate operation receives remaining time, never a fresh whole timeout.
Inject clock/process interfaces for deterministic boundary tests. Retain cumulative
resource baselines; resource/timeout abort cannot become PASS.

Track exact child handles, readers/writers and run-bound remote ownership identities
from creation, including partial startup. Stop admission, attempt graceful cleanup,
then only authorized owned-resource escalation within the deadline. Blocking I/O and
collection must be cancellable or isolated behind a bounded supervised boundary.
Retain uncertain ownership at deadline. Parent death requires independent remote
run-scoped supervision/lease, whose identity/privileges need separate review.

SSH exit is not remote cleanup proof. Require fresh run-bound evidence per endpoint:
exact source/binary identity, owned process identity with anti-reuse binding, child
reap, released sockets and actual ownership counters. Missing/stale/replayed/wrong-run
or contradictory reports remain UNCONFIRMED. Define independent observer provenance;
this outline does not authorize new signatures, keys or trust mechanisms.

Acceptance cases: partial startup; stalled stdin/stdout/stderr or collection;
terminate/kill/wait failure; disconnect; repeated cancellation in every phase;
deadline exhaustion; resource abort; management-host loss; PID reuse; stale/wrong-run
cleanup evidence. Assert global bound, attempts for all owned resources, retained
uncertainty and no PASS. Deterministic checks precede separately authorized live
fault tests. No implementation, keys, sockets, settings or deployment here.
''',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
rows=[dict(path=p.relative_to(o).as_posix(),bytes=p.stat().st_size,sha256=sha(p.read_bytes())) for p in sorted(o.rglob('*')) if p.is_file() and p.name!='inventory.json'];d=dict(base_commit=base['commit'],tree=base['tree'],baseline_verified_paths=len(names),baseline_byte_recovery=corrections,files=rows,total_bytes=sum(x['bytes'] for x in rows));(o/'inventory.json').write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n');assert all(sha((o/x['path']).read_bytes())==x['sha256'] for x in rows);print(json.dumps(dict(files=len(rows),bytes=d['total_bytes'],inventory_sha256=sha((o/'inventory.json').read_bytes()),patch_sha256=sha((o/'combined-ad77.patch').read_bytes()),disk_free=shutil.disk_usage(o).free)))
